{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum","lean:module:QOU.Mass.C1KernelAsShiftSum"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_residual_kills_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_residual_kills_tower","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L228-L238","doc":"... and hence the whole tower is zero from level `n₀` on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_smul","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L222-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_residual_kills_jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_residual_kills_jet","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L206-L220","doc":"**Under the unit-shift dictionary the kernel cannot carry the residual**: a tower\nalternating from level `n₀` on has a zero jet already at level `n₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_zero_c1E_O_zero_imp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_zero_c1E_O_zero_imp","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L178-L204","doc":"**The two even-part constraints are jointly fatal.** `E Y = 0` reads\n`(q^{e+2} − 1) Y(e+2) = (q − 1) Y(e)`; `E (O Y) = 0` reads the same with `q^{e+1}`.\nSubtracting, `q^{e+1}(q − 1) Y(e+2) = 0` for every `e`, so `Y = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O_smul","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L173-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_smul","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L168-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O_anticomm_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O_anticomm_mono","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L165-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_comm_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_comm_mono","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L160-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_eq_E_add_O","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOp_eq_E_add_O","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L154-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O_apply","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L150-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E_apply","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L145-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1O","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L141-L143","doc":"The odd part of the kernel under (a): the shift-1 term, constant weight `−(q − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1E","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L137-L139","doc":"The even part of the kernel under (a): the shift-2 and zeroth-order terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOpCover_residual_kills_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOpCover_residual_kills_tower","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L125-L133","doc":"**Under the cover dictionary the kernel cannot carry the residual**: a tower\nalternating from level `n₀` on is zero from level `n₀ + 1` on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOpCover_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.c1KernelOpCover_smul","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L119-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.comm_mono_residual_from_level_kills_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.comm_mono_residual_from_level_kills_tower","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L99-L112","doc":"**A monodromy-commuting tower that alternates from level `n₀` on is zero from level\n`n₀ + 1` on.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.map_zero_of_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.map_zero_of_smul","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L93-L97","doc":"A homogeneous operator sends `0` to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.comm_mono_flip_kills","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelDictionaryParity.comm_mono_flip_kills","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelDictionaryParity.lean#L69-L90","doc":"**Two consecutive alternating levels kill the tower.** If `T` commutes with the\ncovering monodromy and is homogeneous, the character of level `n` is transported to\nlevel `n + 1` unchanged; alternation between the two levels then forces\n`2 · (−1)^n ε · Tⁿ⁺¹X = 0`. No hypothesis on the seed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}